Ok I see what you mean now. So you are using underscore prefixed imports as a workaround to mount additional directories to edge runtime container. ie.

```json
    "__workspace": "../../../../../deno.json",
    "__libs": "../../../../../libs",
```

Since we removed traversing of unused imports, this became a breaking change for your use case.

I can update CLI to handle the old behaviour using scopes block instead. for eg. in deno.json

```json
{
  "imports": {
    "@faker-js/faker": "npm:@faker-js/faker@^9.8.0"
  },
  "scopes": {
    "__workspace": {
      "__libs": "../../../../../libs"
    }
  }
}
```

@alita-moore could you give `npx supabase@beta functions serve` a try, after updating your deno.json to the following?

```
{
  "imports": {
    "@faker-js/faker": "npm:@faker-js/faker@^9.8.0",
    "@std/assert": "jsr:@std/assert@1",
    "#/": "./src/",
    "express": "npm:express@^5.1.0",
    "formatjs": "npm:formatjs@^0.1.1",
    "jose": "npm:jose@^6.0.11",
    "luxon": "npm:luxon@^3.6.1",
    "zod": "npm:zod@^3.25.67",
    "@db": "../../db/index.ts"
  },
  scopes: {
    "__local": {
      "__workspace": "../../../../../deno.json",
      "__libs": "../../../../../libs",
      "__domain": "../../../../../domain",
    }
  }
}
```

I've verified this on your sandbox. https://codesandbox.io/p/devbox/tender-goldberg-zz898x
